{"result":[{"biographic_references":[],"contributors":{"authors":[{"aliases":[],"checked":"1","codes":["balogh.jozsef"],"name":"Balogh, József"},{"aliases":[],"checked":"1","codes":["linz.william"],"name":"Linz, William"}],"author_references":[],"editors":[]},"database":"Zbl","datestamp":"2024-10-08T09:57:17Z","document_type":{"code":"j","description":"journal article"},"editorial_contributions":[{"language":"English","reviewer":{"author_code":null,"reviewer_id":null,"name":null,"sign":null},"text":"Summary: In this note, we give short proofs of three theorems about intersection problems. The first one is a determination of the maximum size of a nontrivial \\(k\\)-uniform, \\(d\\)-wise intersecting family for \\(n \\geqslant (1+\\frac{d}{2})(k-d+2)\\), which improves the range of \\(n\\) of a recent result of \\textit{J. O'Neill} and \\textit{J. Verstraëte} [J. Comb. Theory, Ser. A 178, Article ID 105369, 13 p. (2021; Zbl 1466.05208)]. Our proof also extends to \\(d\\)-wise, \\(t\\)-intersecting families, and from this result we obtain a version of the Erdős-Ko-Rado theorem for \\(d\\)-wise, \\(t\\)-intersecting families.\n\nOur second result partially proves a conjecture of \\textit{P. Frankl} and \\textit{N. Tokushige} [Extremal problems for finite sets. Providence, RI: American Mathematical Society (AMS) (2018; Zbl 1416.05001)] about \\(k\\)-uniform families with restricted pairwise intersection sizes.\n\nOur third result is about intersecting families of graphs. Answering a question of \\textit{D. Ellis} [Lond. Math. Soc. Lect. Note Ser. 481, 115--173 (2022; Zbl 1532.05160)], we construct \\(K_{s, t}\\)-intersecting families of graphs which have size larger than the Erdős-Ko-Rado-type construction, whenever \\(t\\) is sufficiently large in terms of \\(s\\). The construction is based on nontrivial \\((2 s)\\)-wise \\(t\\)-intersecting families of sets.","contribution_type":"summary"}],"id":7923211,"identifier":"1547.05295","keywords":["nontrivial intersecting family","Hilton-Milner","forbidden intersection","graph intersection"],"language":{"languages":["English"],"addition":[null]},"license":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"],"links":[{"identifier":"10.5070/C64163841","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5070/C64163841"},{"identifier":"2104.00778","type":"arxiv","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.00778"}],"msc":[{"code":"05D05","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Extremal set theory"},{"code":"05D99","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Extremal combinatorics"}],"references":[{"doi":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","position":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","text":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","zbmath":{"author_codes":["ahlswede.rudolf","khachatrian.levon-h"],"document_id":934995,"msc":["05D05"],"prefix":"Zbl","series_id":479,"year":"1996"}},{"doi":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","position":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","text":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","zbmath":{"author_codes":["khachatrian.levon-h","ahlswede.rudolf"],"document_id":986975,"msc":["05D05"],"prefix":"Zbl","series_id":824,"year":"1997"}},{"doi":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","position":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","text":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","zbmath":{"author_codes":["khachatrian.levon-h","ahlswede.rudolf"],"document_id":1604122,"msc":["05D05"],"prefix":"Zbl","series_id":919,"year":"1999"}},{"doi":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","position":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting licenses.","text":"zbMATH Open Web Interface contents unavailable due to conflicting 